                <pb facs="0955" n="875" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg875"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Merry to Mr. Hill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-03-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 698.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your cablegram dated March 14. On receipt thereof I sent a cablegram to the
                    minister of foreign affairs of Salvador, copy of which please find herewith, and
                    also copy of my dispatch to him on the same subject, which goes forward via
                    Puntarenas by mail hence to-morrow.</p>
                <p>With the hope that this claim is now likely to receive a friendly solution in the
                    near future, I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Lawrence
                    Merry.</hi></signed></closer>







